0..71 Comment "// A function written as `fun (q) { e }` acts on a path through `cong`."
72..74 Comment "//"
75..149 Comment "// Whiskering composes each path of a path of paths with a fixed path. The"
150..222 Comment "// function that does it is short, and a stated type for it only repeats"
223..242 Comment "// the path\'s type."
243..245 Comment "//"
246..318 Comment "// The binder takes the type of the path\'s points. Where no path type is"
319..382 Comment "// stated, `cong` reads its own off the path type the body has."
383..385 Comment "//"
386..451 Comment "// - see: #3773 — a lambda as `cong`\'s function, refused before"
452..525 Comment "// - see: #3829 — a lambda where no path type is stated, refused before"
526..596 Comment "// - see: #3919 — a lambda stating its binder\'s type, refused before"
